course: dictionary
lesson: 3032
title: The eardrum
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The eardrum is a thin, tight piece of skin deep inside your ear. «Never push anything like a pencil or hairgrip into your ear; it can hurt the eardrum, the thin skin deep inside the ear that lets you hear.» The sentence tells you where it is and what it is for.
explain: Sound is vibrations travelling through the air. When sound reaches the eardrum, it shakes, or vibrates. Tiny bones pass these vibrations on, and the inner ear sends signals to the brain, so you can hear.
explain: Look at the word parts: ear and drum. A drum has a tight skin that shakes when you hit it, and your eardrum works in a similar way. To check, swap in your meaning: «Doctors say not to put cotton buds in the ear, as they can hurt the thin skin inside.» It still makes sense.
fact: The eardrum is a thin, tight piece of skin inside the ear.
fact: «Eardrum» means a thin, tight piece of skin inside the ear that vibrates when sound reaches it.
fact: Sound travels through the air as vibrations, and the eardrum shakes when they reach it.
fact: «Damage your eardrum» means harm the thin skin so that it cannot hear properly.
fact: Never push cotton buds, pencils or hairgrips into your ear; tell an adult if something is stuck.
exercise: What does eardrum mean? | A bone at the bottom of the ear | *A thin, tight piece of skin inside the ear that vibrates when sound reaches it | A hole in your head where sound escapes
exercise: «When sound reaches the eardrum, it does what?» Pick the right answer. | *Shakes, which is called vibrating | Freezes solid | Turns into light | Shrinks away for ever
exercise: Why should you never push a hairgrip into your ear? | It keeps the ear warm | It makes your hearing louder for ever | *It can hurt the thin skin of the eardrum that lets you hear
test: «Cotton buds pushed into the ear can damage the eardrum.» Find and copy the word that names the thin skin inside the ear. | cotton | pushed | *eardrum | ear
test: Why do doctors say not to push cotton buds into your ears? | To keep the ears warm | Because they are too small to see | To make the eardrum shake faster | *Because they can push wax deeper or hurt the eardrum
exam: «Glue ear is sticky fluid left behind the eardrum after a cold that muffles sound.» What does muffles mean here? | *Makes sound quieter and harder to hear | Stops the eardrum from ever shaking again | Turns sound into music | Makes sound louder and clearer
